// ===========================================================================
// OBESITY — LAYERED. The CONVENTION: histories -> named selections -> derivations.
//
// ⭐ ONE OF THREE LEGITIMATE AUTHORING OPTIONS (operator, 2026-08-29), and the
// one we expect to establish as the convention. Assume an Obesity LIBRARY whose
// every layer some other library consumes.
//
// ⭐ THE RULE THAT SHAPES IT: you never add a "Height". You add a HEIGHT RECORD.
// So the history is the ANSWER SLOT — the only place a local `code is` belongs —
// and every Record above it is a NAMED SELECTION, derived and never answered.
// The names say so: `Most Recent Height`, not `Height`.
//
// That is what makes the layer earn its keep rather than being a restatement:
// `Most Recent Weight` and `Greatest Weight` are two selections over ONE history,
// and neither restates the code or the source representation.
//
// ⚠ Contrast the other two options, which conflate the two roles on one concept:
// a coded Record is simultaneously the answer slot AND a selection, and its
// selection is implicitly "most recent" — so a SECOND selection (a greatest, an
// earliest) has nowhere to attach without reducing something already reduced.
//
// ⚠ OPEN, and this file is where it shows: a derivation and a recorded history
// are two arms of one determination, and nothing here merges them. See `BMI`.
// Deliberately left unresolved rather than papered over.
// ===========================================================================
library "Obesity Coverage (Layered)".

terminology "Obese VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/vitals/ValueSet/obese`.
terminology "Clinical BMI VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/vitals/ValueSet/bmi`.
terminology "Height VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/vitals/ValueSet/height`.
terminology "Weight VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/vitals/ValueSet/weight`.

// ── LAYER 1 — the HISTORIES ────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The ANSWER SLOTS. A local `code is` lives here and nowhere else: answering
// means adding a record, so an answer is in the history by construction and the
// history is never a partial account of itself.

concept "Height Records":
- shape is RecordSet.
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- code is `height`.
- source representation:
  - type is Observation.
  - coded from "Height VS".

concept "Weight Records":
- shape is RecordSet.
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- code is `weight`.
- source representation:
  - type is Observation.
  - coded from "Weight VS".

concept "BMI Records":
- shape is RecordSet.
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- code is `bmi`.
- source representation:
  - type is Observation.
  - coded from "Clinical BMI VS".

concept "Obese Records":
- shape is RecordSet.
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `obese`.
- source representation:
  - type is Condition.
  - coded from "Obese VS".
  - value projection is exists this.

// ── LAYER 2 — the NAMED SELECTIONS ─────────────────────────────────────────
// Records. Each names ONE reduction of ONE history. No code, no posrep: a
// selection is not a thing you answer, and the datum was already described once
// below. ⭐ `Most Recent Weight` and `Greatest Weight` are the point of the
// layer — two selections, one history, nothing restated.

concept "Most Recent Height":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- definition is most recent "Height Records".

concept "Most Recent Weight":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- definition is most recent "Weight Records".

concept "Greatest Weight":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- definition is highest "Weight Records".

concept "Most Recent Recorded BMI":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- definition is most recent "BMI Records".

// ── LAYER 3 — the DERIVATIONS ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// Computed from the selections. Uncoded, like the selections: a derivation is
// not answered either — what a user answers is the history it competes with.

// ⚠ THE OPEN ONE. This determination has TWO arms — the calculation below, and
// the recorded/answered history reached through `Most Recent Recorded BMI` — and
// nothing in the language merges them into one Record. On the coded-Record
// options that merge is what `, then most recent this` does over a concept's OWN
// records; a derivation with no records of its own has no equivalent. Left
// unresolved on purpose: papering over it would hide the gap this file exposes.
concept "BMI":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- definition is body mass index of "Most Recent Weight" and "Most Recent Height".

// The same two-arm question as BMI: the threshold, versus what was asserted or
// recorded in `Obese Records`.
concept "Obese":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- definition is "BMI" at least 30 'kg/m2'.

activity "Approve Bariatric Surgery":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `APPROVED`.

activity "Deny Bariatric Surgery":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `NOT APPROVED`.

decision "Bariatric Surgery Coverage":
first:
- when "Obese" then recommend activity "Approve Bariatric Surgery".
- otherwise then recommend activity "Deny Bariatric Surgery".
